&lt;p data-start=&quot;150&quot; data-end=&quot;240&quot;&gt;Shape how Graphcore products move from hardware design into reliable volume manufacturing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;242&quot; data-end=&quot;471&quot;&gt;As Staff Manufacturing Product Engineer, you will support NPI development and volume production across complex hardware products. You will connect design, test, quality and supply chain decisions with real manufacturing outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;473&quot; data-end=&quot;671&quot;&gt;Your work will help ensure products are manufacturable, resilient and ready for supplier capability. You will provide DfM feedback that improves PCB and system design before issues reach production.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;673&quot; data-end=&quot;878&quot;&gt;You will work closely with contract manufacturers, especially during NPI and early volume manufacture. You will drive yield improvement, analyse production data and resolve L6 and L10 manufacturing issues.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;880&quot; data-end=&quot;1082&quot;&gt;This role suits someone who enjoys practical engineering ownership across design and production. You will travel to Taiwan and work close to suppliers shaping next generation manufacturing technologies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;1084&quot; data-end=&quot;1104&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The team and culture&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;1106&quot; data-end=&quot;1291&quot;&gt;You will join the Manufacturing and Technology Process team within Operations. The team works across Bristol, Cambridge and Taiwan, close to foundry, package assembly and PCBA partners.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;1293&quot; data-end=&quot;1472&quot;&gt;Work happens through clear ownership, supplier engagement and fast feedback into design teams. You will sp

&lt;h1 class=&quot;PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer&quot; data-section-id=&quot;cxqrzp&quot; data-start=&quot;206&quot; data-end=&quot;221&quot;&gt;About the job&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;223&quot; data-end=&quot;296&quot;&gt;Build the test systems that help deliver AI hardware at production scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;298&quot; data-end=&quot;522&quot;&gt;As a Staff Hardware System Test Engineer, you&#39;ll develop manufacturing test solutions for complex compute systems. Your work will help ensure products reach customers with the quality and reliability expected from Graphcore.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;524&quot; data-end=&quot;749&quot;&gt;You&#39;ll shape how hardware is tested across Host Processor Modules, server blades, and multi-node racks. The tools, test content, and diagnostics you create will directly influence manufacturing efficiency and product quality.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;751&quot; data-end=&quot;978&quot;&gt;You&#39;ll develop test software, design test approaches, and solve challenging hardware issues. You&#39;ll work closely with hardware, firmware, software, and manufacturing teams to improve test coverage and diagnose problems quickly.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;980&quot; data-end=&quot;1236&quot;&gt;This role offers broad technical scope across silicon, boards, systems, software, and manufacturing. You&#39;ll have the opportunity to influence engineering decisions and raise technical standards across the organisation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1 data-section-id=&quot;80lep1&quot; data-start=&quot;1238&quot; data-end=&quot;1260&quot;&gt;The team and culture&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;1262&quot; data-end=&quot;1503&quot;&gt;The Product Test and Diagnosis team owns the strategy for finding and diagnosing hardware defects throughout the product lifecycle. The team works across silicon, boards, servers, and rack-scale systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;1505&quot; data-end=&quot;1724&quot;&gt;Day to da

&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the job&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot; data-start=&quot;150&quot; data-end=&quot;238&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Build the cloud platform that turns Graphcore AI systems into usable, scalable services.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot; data-start=&quot;240&quot; data-end=&quot;484&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Graphcore needs a Bristol-based Staff Cloud Engineer to develop and deploy private and public cloud services for AI compute. You will join the Cloud Platform team within Software Platform, close to datacentre operations and product development.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot; data-start=&quot;486&quot; data-end=&quot;698&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Your work will shape how internal users and customers access large-scale AI systems. You will keep critical infrastructure available while helping pre-release hardware and software become reliable cloud services.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot; data-start=&quot;700&quot; data-end=&quot;956&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;You will operate and extend OpenStack-based services, automate deployment with infrastructure-as-code, and improve observability across the fleet. You will benchmark, validate and optimise systems spanning Graphcore hardware, servers, switches and storage.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot; data-start=&quot;958&quot; data-end=&quot;1160&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;This role suits someone who wants ownership of hard infrastructure problems, not a narrow ticket queue. Expect unproven components, direct user feedback, and decisions that move quickly into production.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
